    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0243" n="135" xml:id="pg135"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports that the <hi rendition="#italic">Aquidaban</hi> ran the
                    forts in the morning under a heavy fire and joined the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Republica</hi>, which was standing off the port, and that it is expected
                    that she will soon bring back troops. He thinks it possible that an engagement
                    will take place near Bahia, where the Government fleet is stationed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
